  "id": "COMPOUND:15007 - PROTEIN:6341",
  "verbalization": "Clematernoside D is shown to have a target relationship with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which in turn is targeted by Antrocinnamomins A and 2''o-Acetylpolygalcin D, both of which target EZH2/SUZ12/EED/RBBP7/RBBP4. This suggests a potential pathway where Clematernoside D may influence the activity of these histone methyltransferases through the intermediate of the phosphatase LC-PTP. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent relationship, with varying scores reflecting the confidence in the connections. The mechanisms appear to involve the modulation of EZH2/SUZ12/EED/RBBP7/RBBP4 through the phosphatase LC-PTP, possibly by altering their activity or interaction with other proteins. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility of a broader regulatory network involving these targets, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
